percona-server (8.0.44-35~int02) unstable; urgency=medium

  * [INT02] BP: detect the number of physical/logical CPUs
  * BUG#28590993: MySQL generates GTID gaps because of option replica-skip-errors
  * PS-10232 [8.0]: Fix performance regression by limiting `rows_in_buffer` to query `LIMIT`
  * [INT02] make c++ constants related to replication adjustable
  * [RP012] Small reordering around atomic operations and memory orderings
  * [RP011] Made the variable std::memory_order parameter of std::atomic methods constant
  * [RP010] Fix for that likely() and unlikely() might not work depending on compiler
  * [RP009] crc32_update_uint64() can be inlined
  * [RP008] Eliminate trx_mutex use from purge worker threads
  * [RP007] Changes dict_sys->mutex to rw_lock for innodb_purge_threads scaling performance
  * [RP005] Shards global counters btr_cur_n_non_sea and btr_cur_n_sea to minimize cache coherency cost
  * [RP004] Optimize InnoDB rw_lock s-lock operation cost on high concurrency
  * [RP003] Revives my_hash_*() functions and changes to use HASH instead of std::unordered_[map/set]
  * [RP001] Avoiding to use std::mt19937 for saving CPU data cache
  * [RP000] Initial adjustment. Still just same as the original MySQL

